From c1e857b6d052d0bf2f4772e9c75118a923432b09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 23:58:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 189/189] pmdomain: mediatek: keep MT6897 OVL root clocks ready
 across runtime PM

Prepare distinct ordinary CCF root references for both OVL domains before
any domain initialization or hardware request. OVL0 uses ovl0; OVL1 uses
both ovl0 (its gate ancestry) and its vendor functional root ovl1. Validate
the complete required pair, providers, IDs and shared voter before prepare.
Runtime callbacks enable prepared roots before HWV-on, and release only
after successful off acknowledgement. Preserve earlier successful root
enables if a later enable fails.

Scope the lifecycle through explicit MT6897 SoC/domain data. Keep parent
readiness and successful clock enables on uncertain transition failures,
and quarantine all controller callbacks to prevent ancestor unwind. After
initialization failure, keep the controller bound without a consumer
provider, retaining its state and rejecting global unused-domain work;
pure preparation failures unwind before hardware access. Check genpd
initialization errors before adding domains to the provider state.

Retain inherited mux boot ownership. An off acknowledgement does not prove
physical off and does not transfer boot ownership. Add portable tests for
preflight cleanup, root sharing, transition errors and quarantine behavior.

